ne L3' covering (1,4) and (3,3). Then we need to cover (2,2) elsewhere.\n\nLet's try a new assignment:\n\n- L1: (1,2)-(2,4) slope 2 (sunny). Covers (1,2),(2,4).\n- L2: (1,3)-(3,2) slope -0.5 (sunny). Covers (1,3),(3,2).\n- L3: (1,4)-(3,3) slope -0.5 (sunny). Covers (1,4),(3,3).\n- L4: (1,5)-(2,2) slope -3 (sunny). Covers (1,5),(2,2).\n\nNow we have covered: column 1 points (1,2),(1,3),(1,4),(1,5) all covered. Column 2 points (2,2),(2,4) covered. Column 3 points (3,2),(3,3) covered. Column 4 point (4,2) not covered. Also column 2 point (2,3) not covered. So we still have (2,3) and (4,2) left.\n\nWe have used all 4 lines. So we need to adjust to include those points.\n\nMaybe we can have a line that covers (2,3) and (4,2). Slope = (2-3)/(4-2) = -1/2 = -0.5, sunny. So a line through (2,3) and (4,2) is sunny. Could we incorporate that line as one of the four lines, perhaps replacing some earlier line? Let's try to incorporate (2,3)-(4,2) as L4. Then we need to cover (1,5) and (2,2) maybe with another line.\n\nLet's try a new assignment:\n\n- L1: (1,2)-(2,4) slope 2 (sunny). Covers (1,2),(2,4).\n- L2: (1,3)-(3,2) slope -0.5 (sunny). Covers (1,3),(3,2).\n- L3: (1,4)-(3,3) slope -0.5 (sunny). Covers (1,4),(3,3).\n- L4: (2,3)-(4,2) slope -0.5 (sunny). Covers (2,3),(4,2).\n\nNow we have covered: (1,2),(1,3),(1,4) (col1). (2,4),(2,3) (col2). (3,2),(3,3) (col3). (4,2) (col4). Uncovered points: (1,5) (col1), (2,2) (col2). That's two points left, but we have no lines left. So we need to adjust again.\n\nMaybe we can have a line that covers (1,5) and (2,2) (slope -3). That could replace one of the earlier lines, perhaps L1. Let's try to replace L1 with (1,5)-(2,2). Then we need to cover (1,2) and (2,4) elsewhere. Could we have a line covering (1,2) and (2,4) (slope 2) as before, but we already used L1 for (1,5)-(2,2). So we need to incorporate (1,2) and (2,4) into some other line, maybe L2 or L3 or L4. Let's see.\n\nWe have L2: (1,3)-(3,2). Could we modify L2 to also pass through